00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.874 line:6% position:50% align:center
Born in London in 1991, Muhammed Khalid

c02
00:00:02.924 --> 00:00:07.531 line:6% position:50% align:center
spent his earliest years in Sierra Leone amid civil war.

c03
00:00:07.581 --> 00:00:12.416 line:6% position:50% align:center
There he learned first-hand what aid and support mean to people in crisis.

c04
00:00:12.466 --> 00:00:17.565 line:6% position:50% align:center
He moved with his mother and grew up in London, carrying that lesson with him.

c05
00:00:17.615 --> 00:00:21.988 line:6% position:50% align:center
In the UAE, he founded AIREV, with early backing from G42's Core42.

c06
00:00:22.038 --> 00:00:27.599 line:6% position:50% align:center
Its platform, SchoolHack, reached over 4 million learners in more than 140 countries,

c07
00:00:27.649 --> 00:00:33.210 line:6% position:50% align:center
touching millions of lives — the kind of support he once saw change lives as a child.

c08
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:38.622 line:6% position:50% align:center
Collaborations with Intel and Qualcomm took UAE-built intelligence further.

c09
00:00:38.672 --> 00:00:44.681 line:6% position:50% align:center
Now Athar carries that purpose wider, putting powerful AI within reach of more people.

c10
00:00:44.731 --> 00:00:47.322 line:6% position:50% align:center
From lived experience to lasting impact.

c11
00:00:47.372 --> 00:00:49.104 line:6% position:50% align:center
Athar — agentic AI for all.

